    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11105" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cōpŭlātīvus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		copulo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to connecting,
				copulative</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">modus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 6, 38, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conjunctiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 3, § 286</span></i>
			, and other gramm. —* <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cōpŭlātīvē</span></b> ,
				<i>connectedly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicere (diequinti),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 4 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			</div>
